meta {
  name: secondary-pan-iocl-card
}

docs {
  # Add a secondary PAN to a torg and create IOCL fuel cards on it, as VAHN_ADMIN

  1. `GET /api/pan/torg/{torgId}/all`: the PANs the torg already has.
  2. `POST /api/pan/torg/{torgId}/additional`: add the secondary PAN. It is verified with the PAN
     provider straight away (a paid call). `panNumber` and `phone` must not be on any other PAN card
     in the system, or it returns statusCode 400.
  3. `POST /api/trucks/attach-to-pan`: link the trucks to the new PAN. IOCL creates the customer from
     the truck's PAN, not the torg's primary PAN, so this step is what makes the secondary PAN count.
     It overwrites any PAN the trucks already had, re-runs the ownership check and queues an
     automatic fuel card creation (IOCL first, then BPCL) for verified trucks with a driver.
  4. `GET /api/trucks/{truckId}`: check the truck now carries the new PAN and is VERIFIED.
  5. `POST /api/fuel-cards/create-card` (VAHN_ADMIN only): create the IOCL card. This is also how you
     retrigger a failed IOCL creation.
  6. `POST /api/trucks/{truckId}/fuel-card?provider=IOCL`: the same creation through the truck route,
     with an optional `alternateMobileNumber`. Steps 5 and 6 are alternatives: by default 5 runs and
     6 skips; pass `plutusApiSecondaryPanUseTruckRoute=true` to run 6 instead.
  7. `GET /api/trucks/{truckId}`: check for an ACTIVE IOCL card.

  Run on staging, passing the VAHN_ADMIN token at run time so it is never stored:

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/secondary-pan-iocl-card --env staging \
        --env-var plutusApiSecondaryPanAdminToken=<VAHN_ADMIN token> \
        --env-var plutusApiSecondaryPanTorgId=<torg id> \
        --env-var plutusApiSecondaryPanNumber=<new PAN> \
        --env-var plutusApiSecondaryPanPhone=<phone unused on any PAN> \
        --env-var plutusApiSecondaryPanTruckId=<truck id in that torg>

  Optional: `plutusApiSecondaryPanHolderName`, `plutusApiSecondaryPanBusinessName`,
  `plutusApiSecondaryPanIoclMobile` (IOCL card mobile; defaults to the driver's phone).
  To skip creating the PAN (it already exists), pass the existing number and run from step 3:
  run the single request files.

  Preconditions: the truck is VERIFIED, has a driver, and the torg has Aadhaar details (IOCL customer
  creation needs them). On staging the IOCL UAT `CreateCustomer` often times out at 30 s and leaves an
  orphaned customer; see knowledge `repos/plutus-java/payments-and-fuel.md` "Orphaned IOCL customer trap".

  Step 5 answering statusCode 400 "Active fuel card already exists for all attempted providers"
  means the queued creation from step 3 already made the card; step 7 shows it.
  Errors from IOCL come back as a generic statusCode 500. Find the cause in Loki with
  `{job="plutus"} |= "for IOCL XtraPower for customer with pan card ID"`.

  All captured values are runtime vars (`bru.setVar`), so nothing is written to the environment file.
  2xx, 400 and 422 come back as HTTP 200 with the real code in the body's `statusCode` (any 2xx
  becomes 200); 5xx keep their HTTP status.
}
